│ patch_description        │ Replace the clipped ring layout and greedy, order-dependent radius computation with a     │
│                          │ deterministic nonlinear constructor. The new constructor starts from several staggered    │
│                          │ hexagonal/layered seeds, then uses SLSQP to optimize all 26 centers and radii             │
│                          │ simultaneously. Its constraints directly encode containment in the unit square and every  │
│                          │ pairwise non-overlap condition.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is substantially stronger than computing radii greedily after choosing centers: the  │
│                          │ previous pair loop can unnecessarily shrink earlier circles and cannot trade radius       │
│                          │ between circles. The staggered rows provide a useful dense initial contact graph, while   │
│                          │ multiple small deterministic perturbations allow the optimizer to break symmetry and      │
│                          │ exploit boundary effects and unequal radii. A final uniform certification scale protects  │
│                          │ against floating-point constraint tolerances, so the returned packing remains valid.      │
