│ patch_name               │ nonlinear_packing_search                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the clipped ring construction with a deterministic nonlinear optimization of all  │
│                          │ circle centers and radii.  The previous outer ring placed many centers nearly on the      │
│                          │ boundary and then clipped them together, leaving very small radii.  The new constructor   │
│                          │ starts from feasible staggered hexagonal/layered arrangements, then uses SLSQP to         │
│                          │ maximize the radius sum subject directly to every boundary and pairwise non-overlap       │
│                          │ constraint.                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Two complementary layered initial layouts are used because boundary effects make a        │
│                          │ perfectly symmetric lattice unnecessarily restrictive.  The best result is selected.  A   │
│                          │ final global feasibility scaling removes numerical constraint tolerances, ensuring all    │
│                          │ reported circles are strictly inside the square and pairwise non-overlapping even if the  │
│                          │ optimizer terminates slightly outside a constraint tolerance.  The public interface and   │
│                          │ return values are unchanged.                                                              │
