│ patch_description        │ Expand the deterministic multistart portfolio beyond tiny lattice perturbations. The      │
│                          │ previous ±0.018 perturbations largely remain in the same local contact topology, which    │
│                          │ limits improvement from the staggered hexagonal seed. Add moderate and broad feasible     │
│                          │ perturbations so SLSQP can discover asymmetric boundary layers and alternative neighbour  │
│                          │ graphs.                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For each perturbed center set, compute a uniform feasible starting radius from both wall  │
│                          │ clearance and the closest pair distance. This preserves a strictly feasible initial point │
│                          │ even for broad perturbations, avoiding the numerical difficulty of beginning SLSQP with   │
│                          │ overlapping circles. The original seed and small perturbations are retained, while        │
│                          │ additional starts explore configurations capable of escaping the approximately 2.59 local │
│                          │ optimum.                                                                                  │
