│ patch_description        │ Polish every SLSQP center placement with the exact fixed-center linear program for radii. │
│                          │ Once centers are fixed, all containment and non-overlap conditions are linear in the      │
│                          │ radii: each radius is bounded by its wall clearance and every pair satisfies r_i + r_j <= │
│                          │ distance(i,j). SLSQP can terminate with radii below this LP optimum even when its centers │
│                          │ are strong. Solving this small LP preserves the nonlinear center arrangement while        │
│                          │ recovering radius allocation lost through joint nonlinear optimization termination. The   │
│                          │ existing final global scaling is retained as a numerical safety certification.            │
