│                          │ SLSQP refinement. The first nonlinear solve discovers a contact topology, while the LP    │
│                          │ extracts the best unequal radii supported by those centers. Reintroducing those LP radii  │
│                          │ into SLSQP lets the centers respond to the improved boundary and contact pressures, often │
│                          │ opening small gaps that the original equal-small-radius initialization cannot exploit. A  │
│                          │ final LP then certifies the best radius allocation for the polished centers. The extra    │
│                          │ refinement is applied only to already strong candidates, limiting runtime.                │
