│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ continuation_lp_polish                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Use a continuation strategy rather than trusting one SLSQP pass from each grid            │
│                          │ perturbation.  Variable-radius packings have many nearly degenerate contact graphs: after │
│                          │ the first joint center/radius solve, resolving the exact fixed-center LP exposes the      │
│                          │ preferred allocation of radius among contacts.  Restarting SLSQP from those improved      │
│                          │ centers with a larger iteration budget can release contacts that were prematurely frozen  │
│                          │ in the first solve.  The original seed and first-pass center arrangement are retained as  │
│                          │ candidates, so an unsuccessful nonlinear pass cannot discard a stronger LP arrangement.   │
│                          │ A few extra asymmetric starts explore the important larger perturbation regimes while     │
│                          │ remaining far below the timeout.                                                          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0316                                                                                   │
