│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multiseed_contact_lp                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses one 26-circle six-row hexagonal seed, three random              │
│                          │ perturbations, SLSQP with `maxiter=700`, and LP radius polishing. Its main limitation is  │
│                          │ that the six-row topology can trap the optimizer in a relatively symmetric contact graph  │
│                          │ near 2.61.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version preserves the joint SLSQP-plus-LP strategy but changes the search            │
│                          │ configuration substantially:                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Uses several deterministic contact-graph-aware seeds: `5-5-6-5-5`, `6-5-5-5-5`,         │
│                          │ mirrored row variants, compact six-row hexagonal variants, and                            │
│                          │ 5x5-grid-plus-interstitial-circle seeds.                                                  │
│                          │ - Inserts the extra circle into several different interior cells rather than always the   │
│                          │ same gap.                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Uses analytic Jacobians for all wall and pair-distance constraints, allowing more       │
│                          │ nonlinear iterations efficiently.                                                         │
│                          │ - Starts radii from the exact fixed-center LP solution scaled by `0.88`, instead of a     │
│                          │ uniform small-radius cap.                                                                 │
│                          │ - Uses a larger `maxiter=950`, tighter `ftol=3e-11`, and deterministic asymmetric         │
│                          │ perturbations to explore nearby asymmetric basins.                                        │
│                          │ - Retains exact LP polishing and a tiny safety scaling to guarantee validity.             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0631                                                                                   │
