│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ contact_graph_continuation                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ This constructor combines two complementary packing ideas: a dense square/interstice seed │
│                          │ and staggered hexagonal-layer seeds. Rather than relying only on independent multistart   │
│                          │ SLSQP runs, it uses a contact-graph continuation strategy: each nonlinear candidate is    │
│                          │ first certified and improved with an exact fixed-center radius LP, then several carefully │
│                          │ scaled deterministic center perturbations are restarted from the best LP-derived radius   │
│                          │ pattern.                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The nonlinear stage uses squared-distance contact constraints with an analytic Jacobian,  │
│                          │ making repeated continuation solves substantially cheaper than finite-difference          │
│                          │ optimization. The final LP gives the best nonuniform radii for the selected centers,      │
│                          │ while a final common contraction guarantees strict containment and non-overlap.           │
