│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ deflated_center_relaxation                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Add a dedicated fixed-radius center-relaxation phase between LP certification and the     │
│                          │ final joint nonlinear solve. A nearly jammed joint solve often cannot change its contact  │
│                          │ graph because every center displacement immediately violates a contact. Deflating the LP  │
│                          │ radii slightly creates geometric room; maximizing a common clearance variable then moves  │
│                          │ centers away from walls and active pair contacts in a coordinated way. Restarting the     │
│                          │ existing joint center/radius optimizer from this repositioned configuration can recover   │
│                          │ the radii while reaching a different, potentially better boundary-adapted contact graph.  │
│                          │ This is especially useful for 26 disks, where the best configurations are slightly        │
│                          │ asymmetric and can be inaccessible from a locked layered local optimum.                   │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
