│ patch_name               │ hex_continuation_lp                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The previous constructor used a 5x5 grid plus one interstitial circle, ten jittered       │
│                          │ starts, SLSQP iterations of 600/850, LP radius polishing, and sequential pairwise safety  │
│                          │ repair. This version retains the useful staggered-grid seed portfolio but adds            │
│                          │ boundary-adapted hexagonal layer seeds, vectorizes the nonlinear constraint Jacobian, and │
│                          │ performs deterministic continuation from the best certified arrangement.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The continuation stages use center jitters of 0.004, 0.009, and 0.014 together with       │
│                          │ contracted initial LP radii of 0.85, 0.72, and 0.60. This allows contact graphs to change │
│                          │ without discarding the strongest first-pass solution. The final repair uses a single      │
│                          │ global certificate scale rather than repeated pairwise shrinking, preserving more of the  │
│                          │ LP objective while guaranteeing containment and non-overlap.                              │
